    rep1: 325.30 tok/s

Measured results
----------------
| config | tok/s | spread | peak VRAM | startup |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| ngl=28 t=auto ctx=8192 | 338.55 | 1.2% | 2837 MiB | 2s |
| ngl=27 t=auto ctx=8192 | 321.98 | 2.1% | 2779 MiB | 2s |

Recommended
-----------
  ngl=28 t=auto ctx=8192  ->  338.55 tok/s (spread 1.2%), 2837 MiB peak VRAM
  fastest measured

  For reference the cost model predicted 1106.12 tok/s at --n-gpu-layers 28;
  measured is -69% against that. The measured number is the one to trust.

  Decode is GPU-bound (100% of each token is read from VRAM), where the
  bandwidth roofline does not apply -- it ignores per-token fixed costs.
  Measured 338.55 tok/s is the only meaningful figure here.

